# CASC datamining caches (online client data pulled by tools/encounter_aura_gen
# — hundreds of MB, build-specific, auto-refetched by client.init(); never
# commit. node_modules IS vendored (2.8 MB) so regen needs no npm install,
# but generation itself ALWAYS contacts Blizzard's CDN (client.init()) —
# vendoring buys dependency reproducibility, not offline operation. Only the
# cache stays out.
/cache/
tools/encounter_aura_gen/cache/
# the regen tool's manifest + lockfile ARE tracked (line-1/2 global ignores
# exempted), and so is every vendored dependency's package.json — without
# those manifests Node can't resolve ESM exports (a fresh checkout fails
# with ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND).
!tools/encounter_aura_gen/package.json
!tools/encounter_aura_gen/package-lock.json
!tools/encounter_aura_gen/node_modules/**/package.json
